# PROTECTION, EMPOWERMENT OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

REGIONAL GAZETTE OF CIREBON REGENCY

NUMBER 1 OF 2018 SERIES E.1

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF CIREBON REGENCY

NUMBER 1 OF 2018

CONCERNING

PROTECTION, EMPOWERMENT OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF CIREBON,

Considering:







a. that children are a trust and gift from Almighty God in whom inherent dignity and worth as complete human beings, and are the next generation of the nation's ideals and struggles, therefore they need to receive protection and the widest possible opportunity for survival, growth and development in a proper manner;
b. that in connection with the many women and children who need protection from various forms of violence, maltreatment, exploitation, and neglect, it is deemed necessary to have strategic efforts from the Regional Government and other parties who are obliged to provide protection to the said women and children;
c. that discrimination and violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights and crimes against humanity, therefore in order to fulfill the constitutional rights of women and children as referred to in letter b, the Regional Government may carry out integrated coordination functions for the implementation of its duties, authorities, and responsibilities;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection, Empowerment of Women and Children.

In View of:







1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 14 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions Within the Province of West Java (State Gazette dated August 8, 1950) as amended by Law Number 4 of 1968 concerning the Establishment of Purwakarta Regency and Subang Regency by amending Law Number 14 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions Within the Province of West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1968 Number 3, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2851);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235), as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297);
4. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
5. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
6. Law Number 36 of 2009 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 144, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5063);
7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 224, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
8. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
9. Presidential Regulation Number 69 of 2008 concerning the Task Force for the Prevention and Handling of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons;
10. Regulation of the Minister of Social Affairs Number 102/HUK/2007 concerning the Establishment and Operation of Shelters and Trauma Centers;
11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 02 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;
12. Regulation of the Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 03 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;
13. Regulation of the Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
14. Regional Regulation of Cirebon Regency Number 9 of 2016 concerning the Determination of Concurrent Government Affairs that are the Authority of the Cirebon Regency Government (Regional Gazette of Cirebon Regency Year 2016 Number 9, Series D.6);
15. Regional Regulation of Cirebon Regency Number 10 of 2016 concerning Procedures for the Formulation of Regional Regulations (Regional Gazette of Cirebon Regency Year 2016 Number 10, Series E.3);
16. Regional Regulation of Cirebon Regency Number 12 of 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus of Cirebon Regency (Regional Gazette of Cirebon Regency Year 2016 Number 12, Series D.7).

With Mutual Approval

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF CIREBON REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF CIREBON

HAS DECIDED:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION, EMPOWERMENT OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

