# CHAPTER IV

## RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 5

The rights of victims and their families to obtain Facilities in the service process consist of/include:  
a. Right to health recovery and right to psychological recovery from suffering experienced by victims;  
b. Right to legal assistance;  
c. Right to obtain information;  
d. Right to social recovery;  
e. Right to restitution (trafficking, rape);  
f. Right to spiritual services;  
g. Right to reintegration;  
h. Right to shelter services;  
i. Right to an advocate.

#### Article 6

Child victims of acts of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 5, also obtain special rights, as follows:  
a. Right to respect and full use for survival, growth and development;  
b. Right to basic services;  
c. Right to equal protection;  
d. Right to be free from various stigma; and  
e. Right to obtain freedom.

# CHAPTER V

## OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

#### Article 7

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection and Empowerment for women and children are the joint responsibility of:  
a. Government/Regional Government and Government Institutions;  
b. Private Sector and Community Institutions;  
c. Society;  
d. Family and or Parents.

#### Article 8

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 7 letter a, include:  
a. Establishing policies for protection, empowerment of women and children;  
b. Implementing policies, protection, empowerment of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;  
c. Conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection and empowerment of women and children;  
d. Providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection and empowerment of women and children;  
e. Allocating budget for the implementation of protection and empowerment of women and children, according to regional financial capacity;  
f. Fostering and supervising the implementation of protection and empowerment of women and children; and  
g. Realizing a child-friendly regency.  
2. In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes programs and action activities for the protection and Empowerment of women and children in the Regional Action Plan as a basis for SKPD in implementing the protection and Empowerment of women and children.  
3. The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), is part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).  
4. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

#### Article 9

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Private Sector and society as referred to in Article 7 letter b, are carried out in the form of community participation and jointly.  
2. The form of participation of the private sector and society as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:  
a. Preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;  
b. Providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to law enforcement or authorized parties; and  
c. Participating in the handling of victims of acts of violence.  
3. The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), is carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 10

The obligations of family and/or parents as referred to in Article 7 letter c and letter d, who legally have full responsibility to prevent all forms of violence and protect women and children as family members.

# CHAPTER VI

## ROLE OF GOVERNMENT, PRIVATE SECTOR AND COMMUNITY INSTITUTIONS

#### Article 11

1. To prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government conducts empowerment and awareness to families, parents, and society by providing information, guidance and/or counseling and realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.  
2. In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government conducts efforts as follows:  
a. Increasing the number and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;  
b. Providing accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;  
c. Providing employment for women;  
d. Building community participation and concern for the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;  
e. Building and providing an information system that is easily accessible;  
f. Building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children;  
g. Optimizing the integrated service center for women and children empowerment (P2TP2A) or other designation as a post for protection of women and children from acts of violence; and  
h. Opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children based on community.

#### Article 12

1. Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 11, is carried out by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:  
a. Social;  
b. Health;  
c. Education;  
d. Manpower;  
e. Women's empowerment and child protection;  
f. Mental and spiritual; and  
g. peace and order.  
3. Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

# CHAPTER VII

## SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 13

1. Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, are as follows:  
a. Complaint services;  
b. Health services;  
c. Legal servicesd. Repatriation;  
e. Recovery, social reintegration, and medicolegal;  
f. Identification services;  
g. Psychological services; and  
h. Shelter.  
2. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), are carried out in accordance with minimum service standards established by the Government and implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:  
a. Social;  
b. Economyc. Health;  
d. Women's empowerment and child protection; and  
e. Mental and spiritual.  
3. In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with Government Agencies, other Regional Governments, and society.  
4. Further provisions regarding the procedures for handling services for women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2) and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

#### Article 14

1. The Regional Government is obliged to provide complaint services for protection, empowerment of women and children.  
2. The Regional Government and society or social service institutions may establish recovery houses or safe houses.

#### Article 15

Further provisions regarding complaint services and social services as referred to in Article 14 shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

# CHAPTER VIII

## INSTITUTIONAL

#### Article 16

1. In the context of providing protection services to women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment (P2TP2A) or other designation as an integrated service center in the protection of women and children from acts of violence including victims of acts of violence.  
2. The Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment (P2TP2A) or other designation as referred to in paragraph (1), functions as a leading sector for integrated service centers in providing protection to women and children from acts of violence.  
3. Further provisions regarding the organization and working procedures of the Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment (P2TP2A) or other designation as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be stipulated by Regent Regulation.
